// player inventory, weapons, firing and single-player gamerules
//
// from dlls/weapons.cpp (CBasePlayerWeapon, FireBullets), crowbar.cpp,
// glock.cpp, python.cpp, mp5.cpp, shotgun.cpp, items.cpp
// (CBasePlayerItem::Touch, CBasePlayerAmmo) and singleplay_gamerules.cpp, plus
// cl_dll/ammo.cpp for the bucket/selection UI. one table plus a fire-mode id
// per attack replaces the SDK's per-weapon class; a row carries both attacks.
//
// projectiles: hl_entities is sized to the parsed map and cannot allocate at
// runtime, so this file owns hl_proj[HLPROJ_MAX], mirroring CGrenade
// (dlls/ggrenade.cpp), CCrossbowBolt, CRpgRocket, CTripmineGrenade,
// CSatchelCharge, CSqueakGrenade and CHornet. a saturated pool drops the shot.
//
// the per-frame tick runs off hl_hud_weapon_hook, the pointer HLHud.ZC declares
// and HL1.ZC calls once per rendered frame through HLHudDraw: single-pass
// compiler, so HLHud.ZC cannot name anything in this file. the view comes out
// of CHLCanvas; the clock is hl_ent_time, the server clock HLEntFrame advances,
// not the render clock.
//
// reload foley comes from the VIEW MODEL's animation events, code 5004
// (HLWeaponVmEvents). only three retail view models carry 5004:
//
//   v_9mmhandgun  reload f4 items/9mmclip2.wav, f23 items/9mmclip1.wav
//   v_9mmar       reload f5 items/cliprelease1.wav, f24 items/clipinsert1.wav
//   v_357         reload f70 weapons/357_reload1.wav
//
// every other view model carries only 5001 muzzle flashes, so the rest is
// emitted here through CHLWeaponInfo.reload_snd and .pump: the shotgun's cock
// (weapons/scock1.wav, CShotgun::ItemPostFrame m_flPumpTime) and the crossbow's
// reload (weapons/xbow_reload1.wav, CCrossbow::Reload).
//
// absent: inventory across a changelevel; the python's zoom, multiplayer only
// in the SDK. item pickups live in HLEntity.ZC, not the inventory table.

